Netmask
In an IP address, there are network bits and host bits
Host bit represents the number
a netmask 255.255.255.0 says that first 3 parts belong to same network and last part is for the hosts
For 192.168.1.42 with mask 255.255.255.0, the network is 192.168.1.0
For 10.10.25.18 with mask 255.255.0.0 the network is 10.10.0.0
